# AI code CLI assistants — the landscape (2025–2026)
#
# tools that operate in the terminal, read your codebase, edit files,
# run commands, and handle multi-step coding tasks autonomously.
# distinct from IDE plugins (Copilot in VS Code) or chat UIs (Claude.ai).


# --- major lab CLIs (full agentic) ---

# Claude Code (Anthropic)
# - the benchmark for agentic CLI coding assistants
# - full codebase context, file editing, shell execution, multi-step tasks
# - powered by Claude (Sonnet / Opus)
# - https://claude.ai/code

# Codex CLI (OpenAI)
# - released April 2025; similar agentic approach to Claude Code
# - powered by o3 / o4-mini
# - https://github.com/openai/codex

# Gemini CLI (Google)
# - released June 2025
# - powered by Gemini 2.5 Pro
# - generous free tier at launch
# - https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli


# --- github / microsoft ---

# GitHub Copilot CLI  (gh copilot)
# - lighter weight than the agentic tools above
# - focused on: explain this command, suggest a shell command
# - not a full agentic coding assistant
# - requires GitHub Copilot subscription
# - gh extension install github/gh-copilot


# --- aws ---

# Amazon Q Developer CLI
# - AWS-flavored; strongest for AWS-specific work
#   (CloudFormation, CDK, Lambda, IAM)
# - formerly part of the CodeWhisperer lineage
# - https://aws.amazon.com/q/developer/


# --- xAI ---

# Grok Build (xAI)
# - launched May 2026; terminal-native, multi-agent
# - up to 8 parallel subagents in isolated git worktrees
# - requires SuperGrok / X Premium+ subscription
# - TypeScript
# - https://x.ai/news/grok-build-cli


# --- open source / model-agnostic ---

# OpenCode
# - most-starred open-source coding agent (~180K GitHub stars, Jul 2026)
# - written in Go — fast, single binary, no runtime dep
# - MIT license; TUI-based with LSP integration for 20+ languages
# - 75+ LLM providers from one config file; MCP support
# - ships via npm, Homebrew, AUR, Nix
# - note: Anthropic forced removal of Claude Pro/Max subscription login
#   in Jan 2026; still works with a raw Claude API key
# - https://github.com/sst/opencode

# Aider
# - model-agnostic: works with Claude, GPT-4, Gemini, local models (Ollama)
# - git-native: commits as it edits, strong for multi-file changes
# - 100+ model support; repo-map intelligence for large codebases
# - good choice if you want model flexibility or self-hosting
# - pip install aider-chat
# - https://aider.chat

# Goose (Block / Square → Linux Foundation)
# - open-source agent CLI, donated to Linux Foundation 2026
# - primarily Rust + TypeScript; extensible via MCP / plugins
# - 70+ MCP extensions, 15+ AI providers including Ollama
# - https://github.com/block/goose

# OpenHands (formerly OpenDevin)
# - autonomous end-to-end: open issue → investigate → write fix → run tests → open PR
# - more hands-off than most; suited to longer autonomous tasks
# - https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands

# Plandex
# - built for very large multi-step tasks (up to 2M token context)
# - diff-review sandbox before applying changes
# - MIT; ~15K stars
# - ⚠️ effectively maintenance-mode since Oct 2025; Plandex Cloud winding down
# - https://github.com/plandex-ai/plandex

# Cline
# - VS Code extension primarily, but has headless CLI / CI mode
# - free, open source, supports any LLM API
# - https://github.com/cline/cline

# Pi (by Armin Ronacher + Mario Zechner)
# - newer minimal framework; token-efficient design
# - Armin Ronacher = Flask creator; respected provenance
# - watch this space


# --- implementation languages ---
#
# Claude Code (Anthropic)     TypeScript / Node.js
# Codex CLI (OpenAI)          Rust  (rewrote from TypeScript; now ~96% Rust, codex-rs)
# Gemini CLI (Google)         TypeScript / Node.js
# Grok Build (xAI)            TypeScript
# GitHub Copilot CLI          Go  (part of the gh CLI ecosystem)
# Amazon Q Developer CLI      Rust
# Mistral Vibe CLI            unknown / Apache 2.0
# OpenCode                    Go  (fast TUI, single binary)
# Aider                       Python  (ML ecosystem is Python-native)
# Goose (Block)               Rust + TypeScript
# Plandex                     Go
# Cline                       TypeScript  (VS Code extension)
# Kimi Code (MoonshotAI)      TypeScript
# Qwen Code (Alibaba)         TypeScript
# ZCode / z.ai (Zhipu)        Node.js / TypeScript
#
# note: Google launched a closed-source Go-based Antigravity CLI in Jun 2026;
# Gemini CLI remains open-source on GitHub under Apache 2.0.
#
# Rust: winning for perf-focused rewrites (Codex) and new entrants (Amazon Q,
# Goose) — single static binary, fast startup, no runtime dep.
# Go: strong for community open-source tools (OpenCode, Plandex, Copilot CLI).
# TypeScript: dominates where iteration speed and npm ecosystem matter.
# Python: Aider — natural fit for the ML/AI library ecosystem.


# --- europe ---

# Mistral Vibe CLI (Mistral AI, France)
# - Apache 2.0, open source; pairs with Devstral 2 (their coding model)
# - the EU-sovereignty play: only frontier-class coding CLI that keeps
#   data inside EU infrastructure
# - https://github.com/mistralai/mistral-vibe


# --- chinese players (emerging, moving fast) ---

# Kimi Code (MoonshotAI)
# - TypeScript, MIT license, open source
# - runs on Kimi K3 (2.8T MoE, 1M context window)
# - built-in coder / explore / plan subagents in isolated contexts
# - MCP support; successor to kimi-cli
# - https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-code

# Qwen Code (Alibaba / QwenLM)
# - TypeScript (React/ink for terminal rendering), Apache 2.0
# - model-agnostic: works with OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or Qwen APIs
# - 1,000 free requests/day; no token cap on free tier
# - IDE plugins + Telegram / DingTalk / WeChat / Feishu bots
# - https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code

# ZCode / z.ai (Zhipu AI — GLM model family)
# - GLM-4.6, 4.7, GLM-5 model family
# - z.ai CLI: Node.js / npx, MCP-integrated, lightweight
# - ZCode: full desktop agentic IDE built on GLM-5
# - https://z.ai

# DeepSeek
# - open-source developer favorite among Chinese labs
# - DeepSeek-Coder-V2: GPT-4 Turbo-level on code tasks, MIT license
# - building their own Claude Code equivalent (watch this space)
# - https://github.com/deepseek-ai

# TRAE (ByteDance / Doubao / Seed models)
# - launched Jan 2025; IDE-focused more than pure CLI
# - Seed 2.1 claimed to match Claude Opus 4.7 on coding benchmarks
# - https://trae.ai

# Baidu Comate
# - enterprise and IDE focused; tight Baidu Cloud integration
# - less CLI-native, stronger on Chinese enterprise market
# - https://comate.baidu.com

# the pattern: Chinese labs are moving fast and mostly forking the
# TypeScript CLI pattern (Claude Code / Gemini CLI). Qwen Code is the
# most notable — genuinely model-agnostic, well-funded, generous free tier.


# --- how they differ ---

# full agentic (read / edit / run / multi-step):
#   Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Grok Build, OpenCode, Aider,
#   Goose, OpenHands, Kimi Code, Qwen Code, ZCode, Mistral Vibe CLI

# command explanation / suggestion (lighter weight, not agentic):
#   GitHub Copilot CLI

# aws-ecosystem specialist:
#   Amazon Q Developer CLI

# eu data sovereignty:
#   Mistral Vibe CLI  (data stays in EU infrastructure)

# model-flexible / self-hostable:
#   OpenCode (75+ providers), Aider (100+ models), Goose, Qwen Code
#   — all pair well with Ollama for local models

# most-starred open source (Jul 2026):
#   OpenCode ~180K, Aider, Goose  (none vendor-owned)

# maintenance-mode / watch-out:
#   Plandex — no commits since Oct 2025, Cloud winding down


# --- maturity & adoption ---
#
# most mature:        Aider — longest track record (2023), battle-tested
#                     across 100+ models, git-native workflow, actively
#                     maintained. the tool people reach for when they want
#                     something that just works with any model.
#
# most widely used:   Claude Code — #1 on Terminal-Bench (Jul 2026);
#                     model and agent co-developed by Anthropic. the de
#                     facto standard every new entrant benchmarks against.
#
# most popular OSS:   OpenCode — ~180K GitHub stars, 7.5M+ monthly active
#                     devs. Go binary, model-agnostic, MIT. the community's
#                     answer to vendor lock-in.
#
# dimension           winner
# ─────────────────── ────────────────────────────────────
# longest track rec.  Aider
# best benchmarks     Claude Code
# largest OSS comm.   OpenCode
# model flexibility   OpenCode / Aider (tied)
# best free tier      Qwen Code (1,000 req/day, no token cap)


